Items Requiring Business/Integration Confirmation
These are not classified as defects without the missing contract evidence:
• Weekend ingestion. The code and four required parameters (HORA_OP_SWF_SA_*, HORA_OP_SWF_DO_*) define Saturday and Sunday windows, but the shared EsDiaHabil() returns false on every Saturday/Sunday unless the general setting FORZA_EJECUCION_SERVICIOS is 1. Confirm whether weekend ingestion is expected; if not, the weekend branches and parameters are dead (MQ-FR-2, MQ-FR-6).
• Actual timer interval. TimerInterval comes from the encrypted service configuration; the host falls back to 10,000 ms when it is null. Per-tick alert, log, and MQ-connection volumes in this report use that default for illustration only.
• Parameter conversion. The procedure declares @mq_msg TEXT while the shared CrearParametro sends a Unicode (nvarchar) value. Run one integration test against the target SQL Server to confirm the conversion succeeds and that non-ASCII message content is preserved (MQ-FR-14).
• Same-ICN, different-payload policy. When the work row for an ICN and type already exists, the procedure ignores the new payload and still returns the ICN. Confirm whether a corrected/re-sent message with the same ICN must be rejected, versioned, or may be dropped (MQ-FR-14).
• Queue-manager facts. Confirm the queue manager platform/version, that a get without MQGMO_SYNCPOINT is non-transactional against the target queue manager (one integration test), whether the service user may rely on a backout queue (BOQNAME/BOTHRESH), and whether the channel authority records require PUT/INQ on the queue (MQ-FR-8, MQ-FR-15).
• Release line. Confirm which branch is intended for release: CodeReview (syncpoint-based reads, an MQ seam, and repository tests) or the current CodeReview2.
