• Constructor injection and a verified composition root. OperacionServicio.cs (../../SWIFT/Incoming/SWF_IN_MQ/AplicacionSwfINMQ/OperacionServicio.cs#L23-L37) receives every collaborator through its constructor, and ServiceHost.cs (../../SWIFT/Incoming/SWF_IN_MQ/SwfINMQ/ServiceHost.cs#L47-L86) registers them in SimpleInjector and calls Verify(). Configuracion is registered as a scoped clone (line 80 (../../SWIFT/Incoming/SWF_IN_MQ/SwfINMQ/ServiceHost.cs#L80)) and each tick opens its own scope (line 124 (../../SWIFT/Incoming/SWF_IN_MQ/SwfINMQ/ServiceHost.cs#L124)), so per-tick configuration changes never leak between ticks.
• Database access is parameterized. RepositorioTomi.cs (../../SWIFT/Incoming/SWF_IN_MQ/InfraestructuraSwfINMQ/Repositorio/RepositorioTomi.cs#L223-L227) calls a fixed stored-procedure name and binds @tipo_operacion and @mq_msg with CrearParametro; no SQL is built by concatenation anywhere in the solution.
• Secrets stay out of the repository and out of the logs. The MQ password, cipher spec, key repository, and certificate label are requested as required sensitive parameters (ConstantesServicio.cs (../../SWIFT/Incoming/SWF_IN_MQ/AplicacionSwfINMQ/Enums/ConstantesServicio.cs#L13)); the shared loader throws when any is missing or blank and masks sensitive values in its INFO line (Parametrizacion.cs (../../General/MUFGT24_BTMUM_64/MUFG_T24/Aplicacion/Control/Parametrizacion.cs#L241-L258)). App.config holds no secrets, and .gitignore excludes *.pfx, logs, bin/, obj/, and packages/.
