Saturday opens with SA_INI but closes with Wednesday's MI_FIN; HORA_OP_SWF_SA_FIN is required and loaded but never read. The branch is only reachable when the shared EsDiaHabil() returns true on a Saturday, which it does only when the general setting FORZA_EJECUCION_SERVICIOS is 1; otherwise OperacionServicio returns at the non-business-day check (line 68) before the schedule logic runs. The defect is therefore latent in the default configuration and live in forced mode. The same gate makes the Sunday branch unreachable unless forced (see the weekend question in Section 2).
Recommendation: use HORA_OP_SWF_SA_FIN, covered by the same per-weekday test as MQ-FR-1. Decide with the business whether weekend ingestion is intended; if it is, the non-business-day gate must not block it, and if it is not, delete the weekend branches and parameters.
Benefit: removes a wrong-closing-time defect and resolves the contradiction between the weekend parameters and the weekend gate.
MQ-FR-3 - Schedule parse failures silently produce zero or partial windows and misleading diagnostics
• Category / severity: MustChange/rewrite - Major
• Evidence: OperacionServicio.cs (../../SWIFT/Incoming/SWF_IN_MQ/AplicacionSwfINMQ/OperacionServicio.cs#L84-L92), failure logs such as lines 97-105 (../../SWIFT/Incoming/SWF_IN_MQ/AplicacionSwfINMQ/OperacionServicio.cs#L97-L105), and the zero test at lines 175-179 (../../SWIFT/Incoming/SWF_IN_MQ/AplicacionSwfINMQ/OperacionServicio.cs#L175-L179)
Code block (csharp)
DateTime fecha = new DateTime();
if (DateTime.TryParseExact(_configuracion.FechaSistema, "yyyyMMdd", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture, DateTimeStyles.None, out var result))
{
    fecha = result;
}
switch (fecha.DayOfWeek) { ... }
...
if (TimeSpan.TryParse(_configuracion.ParametrosSistema[ConstantesServicio.HORA_OP_SWF_LU_INI], out var Monday))
    horaInicio = Monday;
else
    Config.EscribirLog($"{ConstantesClaveAviso.Error}|{ConstantesServicio.ErrorHora}:{Monday}.");
...
if (horaInicio == TimeSpan.Zero && horaFin == TimeSpan.Zero) { ... return false; }
Four related defects share this block:
1. new DateTime() is 0001-01-01, which is a Monday. If the business-date string ever fails to parse, the failure is ignored and Monday's window is applied with no error. Today this is masked because the shared ObtenerFechaSistemaAsync always formats a DateTime as yyyyMMdd (Parametrizacion.cs (../../General/MUFGT24_BTMUM_64/MUFG_T24/Aplicacion/Control/Parametrizacion.cs#L146)); any change in that contract becomes a silent wrong-day schedule.
2. On a failed TimeSpan.TryParse the code logs the out variable (Monday, MondayFin, ...), which is always 00:00:00 after a failure, instead of the configured text, so the log never identifies the bad value (14 sites).
3. Only a failure of *both* boundaries is reported. If only the start fails it stays 00:00 and the window silently widens to midnight-to-end; if only the end fails it stays 00:00, every tick is "out of hours", and the alert says "fuera de horario" instead of naming the configuration error.
4. The out-of-window test now < inicio || now > fin is true for every time of day when inicio > fin, so an overnight window can never be in effect: the service is always treated as out of hours, with no validation or message.
Recommendation: fail the cycle explicitly with a Critical alert naming the key and the raw value when either boundary or the business date is invalid; parse with an explicit format; reject inicio >= fin unless overnight windows are deliberately supported; and check the TryParseExact result and fail explicitly for the business date (the shared ObtenerFechaSistemaValidadaAsync only rejects a null value, not a malformed one). These checks belong in the single parser proposed in MQ-FR-6.
Benefit: configuration errors become visible, immediate, and attributable instead of silently shifting the processing window.
MQ-FR-4 - Execution state is finalized only on the successful path (GEN-7)
• Category / severity: MustChange/rewrite - Major
• Evidence: start mark at OperacionServicio.cs (../../SWIFT/Incoming/SWF_IN_MQ/AplicacionSwfINMQ/OperacionServicio.cs#L55), early returns at lines 60, 82, 178, and 198 (../../SWIFT/Incoming/SWF_IN_MQ/AplicacionSwfINMQ/OperacionServicio.cs#L198), the only finalization at line 207 (../../SWIFT/Incoming/SWF_IN_MQ/AplicacionSwfINMQ/OperacionServicio.cs#L207), and the catch at lines 212-227 (../../SWIFT/Incoming/SWF_IN_MQ/AplicacionSwfINMQ/OperacionServicio.cs#L212-L227); procedure semantics in start (../../StoredProcedures/MWD_DB/DBMDW/General/MUFG_T24_BTMUM_64/IT24/Procedures/001%20SP%20usp_ActualizaEjecucion_MUFGLibreria.sql) (status = 1) and end (../../StoredProcedures/MWD_DB/DBMDW/General/MUFG_T24_BTMUM_64/IT24/Procedures/007%20SP%20usp_ActualizaTerminacion_HotScan.sql) (status = 0)
Code block (csharp)
var resultadoEjecucion = await _controlServicio.ActualizaEJecucion(_configuracion.NombreServicio, ct); // status = 1
...                                                   // non-business day, bad schedule, off-hours: return false
var respuesta = await _repositorioTomi.ObtieneLecturaMensajesMQ();
await _controlServicio.ActualizaTerminacion(_configuracion.NombreServicio, ct);                          // status = 0, success path only
return respuesta;
...
catch (Exception ex) { ... await _alertas.InsertarAlerta(...); }                                         // no finalization
Every tick writes tb_srv_controladoradeservicios.status = 1 before validating anything, but only the path that reaches line 207 writes status = 0. Non-business days, invalid schedules, off-hours ticks, and every exception leave the persisted state marked as running; the host adds a final ActualizaTerminacion only at service shutdown (ServiceHost.cs (../../SWIFT/Incoming/SWF_IN_MQ/SwfINMQ/ServiceHost.cs#L178)). Anything that reads that table (monitoring, controller services) therefore sees this service as "running" through nights and weekends and after failures. If the finalizer reused the already-cancelled ct it would also fail, because the shared method calls ct.ThrowIfCancellationRequested() and rethrows cancellation (RepositorioMaestro.cs (../../General/MUFGT24_BTMUM_64/MUFG_T24/Infraestructura/Repositorios/DBs/RepositorioMaestro.cs#L1193-L1230)).
Recommendation: wrap the tick in try/finally, compute an explicit outcome (Succeeded, Skipped, Failed, Cancelled), and call ActualizaTerminacion in the finally with a short independent token (the host's cleanupCt pattern), inspect its result (MQ-FR-16), and never let a finalizer failure replace the primary exception.
Benefit: the persisted run state matches reality after skips, failures, and cancellation.
